 "notes": "Chart 6 spans a single left/right spread (pp.112-113). Left page (p.112) is blank except title, page number, and the printed annotation paragraph; the full 18-column ledger grid is on the right page (p.113), headed 1938. All handwritten entries in this chart fall in the UPWARD TREND columns (black ink, rows Oct.25-Nov.12) and then jump to the NATURAL REACTION columns (blue ink, rows Nov.18-Nov.28) per the printed note about Nov 18. No SECONDARY RALLY, NATURAL RALLY, DOWNWARD TREND, or SECONDARY REACTION entries appear anywhere on this chart. Rows below Dec.8 1938 (through the bottom of the visible grid) are blank/unfilled in the supplied crops. Day-of-week gaps in the date column (e.g. Nov.8, Nov.11, Nov.24 skipped) are consistent with known 1938 NYSE holiday closures (Election Day, Armistice Day, Thanksgiving) plus the every-week Sunday gap; used to sanity-check the isoDate sequence. KP = US + BS checksum was verified exactly for every row where all three instruments have entries (Oct.25, Oct.27, Nov.7, Nov.9, Nov.10, Nov.12, Nov.18, Nov.26, Nov.28); no discrepancies found, so no cell needed uncertain:true.",
